ule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the built reports; must follow all Implementation epics. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n| E001 ⇢ BRANCH-B-E005 | Rule 3 / conditional decomposition | The branch epic is gated by the investigation and exists only in outcome B. |\n| E003 has no dependencies | Rules 14/15 | KFP run metadata is already retained and pipeline runs are already surfaced in the console (data-science-pipelines.md corroborates); no gating unknown, no shared artifact under construction. Starts immediately, in parallel with E001. |\n\nBoundary decisions:\n\n- **E002 and E003 are separate epics** despite sharing component and team: they\n  are separate report surfaces over architecturally distinct data sources\n  (Notebook CR activity data vs. Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata), and only E002\n  is gated by the investigation. Splitting along the data-source boundary keeps\n  the ungated pipeline-run report from being serialized behind the workbench\n  unknown.\n- **CSV export (HLR-3) is bundled into both report epics, not split out**: the\n  export action lives on each report's own UI surface and shares its data, so it\n  is not separately schedulable — a standalone export epic would re-touch both\n  report views (see HLR Traceability Matrix for the row-level rationale).\n- **Documentation is a separate epic** (HLR-4 asks for new doc topics explaining\n  the reports and safe reclamation steps — substantive content authoring, not an\n  incidental touch-up), blocked by both report implementations per Rule 11.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P1 | E001 (enables), E002 | E001 resolves the data-source unknown; E002 delivers the per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking. In outcome B, BRANCH-B-E005 supplies the readable surface E002 consumes. |\n| HLR-2 | P1 | E003 | Per-project stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from KFP run metadata. |\n| HLR-3 | P2 | E002 (bundled), E003 (bundled) — CSV export is an action on each report's own UI surface over the same report data; it shares the surface and data structures of the P1 report work, so it is not a distinct deferrable feature and a split would touch both report views twice. | Each report epic implements export for its own report. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of both reports and safe reclamation steps; docs-authoring priority derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2 (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n\nFull coverage: HLR-1 through HLR-4 all map to at least one epic; no orphaned\nrequirements. Out-of-scope items (automated reclamation, cost/chargeback) are\nexcluded from all epic scopes.\n\n## Investigation Outcomes and Conditional Branches\n\nE001 has two bounded outcomes:\n\n- **Outcome A — last-activity already readable via the Kubernetes API** (e.g.\n  exposed on the Notebook CR status or an equivalent K8s-readable surface): the\n  main plan proceeds unchanged; E002 reads the existing surface. No branch\n  epics.\n- **Outcome B — not readable today**: BRANCH-B-E005 (Notebooks / Workbenches,\n  P1) exposes per-workbench last-activity on a Kubernetes-readable surface so\n  the console can read it without private component APIs. In this outcome the\n  branch epic completes before E002's data wiring consumes the new surface; its\n  culling behavior must be unchanged. Its `gate_failure_impact` is `remove`: if\n  outcome A holds, the epic does not exist.\n\nE002 carries `gated_by: E001` with `gate_failure_impact.action: rewrite` — if\nthe data is not readable, the report's data-source wiring is rebuilt against\nthe surface exposed by the branch work.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n  and no Non-Functional Requirements; its Affected Components section is a bare\n  list without owner teams or change descriptions. Team assignments in this\n  decomposition are derived from the architecture-context owning teams\n  (dashboard.md, notebooks.md, data-science-pipelines.md).\n- **\"Open Questions: None\" vs. an unresolved data-consumption path**: the\n  strategy asserts the workbench activity data \"exists; it is just not surfaced\n  anywhere\", but dashboard.md states the console's interface is\n  \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\", and notebooks.md describes\n  last activity as \"tracked per kernel through Jupyter server API probes\" by\n  the culler, with no stated CR-status exposure. Whether that tracked value is\n  readable through the Kubernetes API is a genuine unknown that changes which\n  epics exist (it determines whether Notebooks-component work is needed), so it\n  is decomposed as Investigation E001 with a conditional branch rather than\n  taken as resolved.\n- **Documentation team assumption**: HLR-4 is assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard\n  team because the strategy names no documentation owner; reassign if a\n  dedicated docs team owns these topics.\n- **Passive-component validation**: the notebook controller (outcome A) and\n  Kubeflow Pipelines are passive — both are covered by read-only-consumption\n  acceptance criteria on E002/E003 respectively (no behavior changes, culling\n  unaffected), not by separate epics.\n- No priority inversions detected: both P1 HLRs are console reports of\n  comparable complexity; the P2 items (CSV export, docs) are correctly\n  subordinate.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable. The strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\ntiming — all data sources are in-platform components, and no upstream\ncontributions or vendor coordination are required.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"inpu