{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-383a4016-dcd9-4799-a773-7ee080dd8689","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae900c836a413407","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-cz58lmf1/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E002.md","content":"# Console idle-workbench report with CSV export\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the per-project idle-workbench report in the RHOAI web\nconsole: an administrator-facing report showing, for each workbench in a\nproject, its last activity, owner, and reserved resources, sourced from the\nnotebook controller's activity tracking. It also delivers CSV export of the\nreport so administrators can export the data for offline use. Cluster\nadministrators use this report to see which workbenches are sitting idle and\nreclaim capacity with confidence; no automated reclamation is performed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- A new administrator-facing report view in the web console, scoped per\n  project, listing workbenches with their last activity, owner, and reserved\n  resources.\n- Data wiring that sources last-activity from the Kubernetes-readable surface\n  identified by the completed workbench-activity data-source investigation; if\n  that investigation found no readable surface, the wiring is built against the\n  surface exposed by the conditional notebook-controller work once it lands.\n- Read-only consumption of notebook-controller data through the Kubernetes API\n  — no private component APIs, no changes to notebook-controller behavior (the\n  idle culler and its configuration remain unaffected).\n- A CSV export action on the report that downloads the currently displayed\n  per-project idle-workbench data.\n- Out of scope: automated reclamation or deletion of idle resources, and\n  cost/chargeback calculations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project with workbenches, the console shows the idle-workbench report\n  listing each workbench with its last activity, owner, and reserved resources.\n- The report's last-activity data is populated from the notebook controller's\n  activity tracking via the Kubernetes API, using the surface identified by the\n  data-source investigation.\n- Notebook-controller behavior is unchanged by this epic: the idle culler\n  continues to operate with its existing configuration (passive-component\n  validation).\n- Administrators can export the idle-workbench report as CSV, and the exported\n  file contains the report's rows and columns.\n- The report is display-only: no reclamation or deletion action is offered.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)** — delivers the per-project idle-workbench report (last\n  activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from the notebook controller's\n  activity tracking.\n- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)** — CSV export of the report is implemented here: the\n  export action lives on this report's own UI surface and shares its data, so\n  it is not separately schedulable from the report itself.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45268,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99f844a42ff9bb63","agent_id":"af98b122f29171fcb","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"4c8e4ee1-4e16-48c9-8bd7-2a3f08f14688","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:22:21.233Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
