ontroller activity tracking, Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata).\n- Screenshots and captions that fall out of the documented flows.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Published documentation explains both reports: what they show, where in the\n  console they appear, and how to read their columns.\n- Published documentation explains how to configure the stale pipeline-run age\n  threshold.\n- Published documentation includes safe reclamation steps for idle workbenches\n  and stale pipeline runs, and clearly states that reclamation is manual.\n- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n  reports (reviewed by the implementing engineers) and validated against the\n  platform architecture context before publication.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P2)** — delivers documentation explaining the reports and safe\n  reclamation steps.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46811,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-99f844a42ff9bb63","agent_id":"af98b122f29171fcb","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"2da951c9-6833-432f-94a0-1b6fb42a66d9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:22:36.307Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
