es integration (KFP v2 run metadata) — read-only\n50\t  consumption, no changes to the Data Science Pipelines component, its\n51\t  operator, or its persistence.\n52\t- A CSV export action on the report that downloads the currently displayed\n53\t  per-project stale-run data.\n54\t- Out of scope: automated reclamation or deletion of runs or artifacts, and\n55\t  cost/chargeback calculations.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, the console shows the stale\n60\t  pipeline-run report listing completed runs older than the configured age,\n61\t  with their retained artifacts indicated.\n62\t- The age threshold is configurable, and changing it changes which runs the\n63\t  report lists.\n64\t- The report's data is populated from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata via the\n65\t  console's existing pipelines integration.\n66\t- The Data Science Pipelines component is unchanged by this epic: run\n67\t  execution, metadata retention, and artifact storage behave exactly as before\n68\t  (passive-component validation).\n69\t- Administrators can export the stale pipeline-run report as CSV, and the\n70\t  exported file contains the report's rows and columns.\n71\t- The report is display-only: no reclamation or deletion action is offered.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — delivers the stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older\n76\t  than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow\n77\t  Pipelines run metadata.\n78\t- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)** — CSV export of the report is implemented here: the\n79\t  export action lives on this report's own UI surface and shares its data, so\n80\t  it is not separately schedulable from the report itself.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bb77dc3f908c610b","agent_id":"ade07d90fd8e81ae9","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"c56de4a3-35b2-488b-802a-9bfb43880873","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:24:15.685Z","tool_res