e type, including cautions about\n53\t  data that may be lost and the explicit statement that reclamation is manual\n54\t  (the platform does not automatically reclaim or delete resources).\n55\t- What is intentionally not covered: automated reclamation and cost/chargeback.\n56\t\n57\t## Scope\n58\t\n59\t- New documentation topics explaining both console reports, their data sources\n60\t  and columns, the configurable age threshold, and safe manual reclamation\n61\t  steps for idle workbenches and stale pipeline runs, per the content outline\n62\t  above.\n63\t- Accuracy validation of every documented claim against the shipped reports\n64\t  and against the platform architecture context (console interfaces,\n65\t  notebook-controller activity tracking, Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata).\n66\t- Screenshots and captions that fall out of the documented flows.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- Published documentation explains both reports: what they show, where in the\n71\t  console they appear, and how to read their columns.\n72\t- Published documentation explains how to configure the stale pipeline-run age\n73\t  threshold.\n74\t- Published documentation includes safe reclamation steps for idle workbenches\n75\t  and stale pipeline runs, and clearly states that reclamation is manual.\n76\t- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n77\t  reports (reviewed by the implementing engineers) and validated against the\n78\t  platform architecture context before publication.\n79\t\n80\t## HLR Traceability\n81\t\n82\t- **HLR-4 (P2)** — delivers documentation explaining the reports and safe\n83\t  reclamation steps.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89bb7d567c197eb1","agent_id":"a1bf09e60a06cbc54","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"4e7035f2-8af6-4716-9f7f-31311051f60c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:29:28.011Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a3f3a9abbdeb5bec","permission_decision":{"decision":