{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc8402237b7615f7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n3\tepic_count: 4\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9016: Idle resource reporting in the web console\n10\t\n11\tStrategy status: Refinement Done. Strategy priority: Normal.\n12\t\n13\tTriage: neither Step 0 check fires. The strategy is not below threshold — it\n14\tspans three affected components and at least two owning teams, and it contains\n15\tmultiple distinct work streams (two console report implementations over\n16\tdifferent backend data sources, plus substantive documentation authoring). It\n17\tis not documentation-only. Full decomposition follows.\n18\t\n19\t## Epic List\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n22\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E001 | Workbench last-activity data source investigation for console reporting | Investigation | Workbenches | P1 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E002 | Console idle-workbench report with CSV export | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E003 | Console stale pipeline-run report with CSV export | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-E004 | Documentation for the idle resource reports and safe reclamation steps | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P2 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9016-BRANCH-B-E005 | Expose workbench last-activity on a Kubernetes-readable surface (conditional, outcome B only) | Implementation | Workbenches | P1 |\n28\t\n29\tMain plan: E001–E004. BRANCH-B-E005 is a conditional branch epic attached to\n30\tthe E001 investigation outcome; it is not a main-plan node.\n31\t\n32\t## Component Mapping\n33\t\n34\tStrategy component names → canonical RHAI Jira components\n35\t(`.context/rhai-components.txt`), with active/passive classification:\n36\t\n37\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Owner team | Classification |\n38\t|--------------------|----------------------|------------|----------------|\n39\t| RHOAI web console | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | Active — both reports are built here |\n40\t| Notebook controller | Notebooks | Workbenches | Passive in outcome A (activity already tracked, no code change); active in branch B (exposure work needed) |\n41\t| Kubeflow Pipelines | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | Passive — run completion metadata is already retained and pipeline runs are already surfaced in the console (data-science-pipelines.md); read-only consumption, validated as an acceptance criterion on E003. No separate validation epic: the consuming team (RHOAI Dashboard) is the validator. |\n42\t\n43\tThe documentation epic uses the canonical `Documentation` component. Team\n44\townership for it is an assumption (see Health Warnings) — the strategy names no\n45\tdoc owner, so it is assigned to the console team whose feature is documented.\n46\t\n47\t## Dependency DAG\n48\t\n49\t```mermaid\n50\tgraph TD\n51\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: workbench activity data source\"] --> E002[\"E002 Idle-workbench report + CSV\"]\n52\t    E002 --> E004[\"E004 Documentation\"]\n53\t    E003[\"E003 Stale pipeline-run report + CSV\"] --> E004\n54\t    E001 -. \"outcome B only (conditional)\" .-> BE005[\"BRANCH-B-E005 Expose last-activity (branch epic)\"]\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\tArrows point from dependency to dependent. The dashed edge is a conditional\n58\tgate, not a main-plan edge: BRANCH-B-E005 exists only if the investigation\n59\tresolves to outcome B, and no main-plan epic depends on it.\n60\t\n61\t## DAG Justification\n62\t\n63\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n64\t|------|------|-----------|\n65\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation edges) | Whether the notebook controller's last-activity data is readable through the Kubernetes API today determines how the report's data wiring is built and whether controller-side exposure work exists. Bounded to two outcomes → conditional branch (below), not phased decomposition. |\n66\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the built reports; must follow all Implementation epics. |\n67\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Same. |\n68\t| E001 ⇢ BRANCH-B-E005 | Rule 3 / conditional decomposition | The branch epic is gated by the investigation and exists only in outcome B. |\n69\t| E003 has no dependencies | Rules 14/15 | KFP run metadata is already retained and pipeline runs are already surfaced in the console (data-science-pipelines.md corroborates); no gating unknown, no shared artifact under construction. Starts immediately, in parallel with E001. |\n70\t\n71\tBoundary decisions:\n72\t\n73\t- **E002 and E003 are separate epics** despite sharing component and team: they\n74\t  are separate report surfaces over architecturally distinct data sources\n75\t  (Notebook CR activity data vs. Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata), and only E002\n76\t  is gated by the investigation. Splitting along the data-source boundary keeps\n77\t  the ungated pipeline-run report from being serialized behind the workbench\n78\t  unknown.\n79\t- **CSV export (HLR-3) is bundled into both report epics, not split out**: the\n80\t  export action lives on each report's own UI surface and shares its data, so it\n81\t  is not separately schedulable — a standalone export epic would re-touch both\n82\t  report views (see HLR Traceability Matrix for the row-level rationale).\n83\t- **Documentation is a separate epic** (HLR-4 asks for new doc topics explaining\n84\t  the reports and safe reclamation steps — substantive content authoring, not an\n85\t  incidental touch-up), blocked by both report implementations per Rule 11.\n86\t\n87\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n88\t\n89\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Coverage |\n90\t|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n91\t| HLR-1 | P1 | E001 (enables), E002 | E001 resolves the data-source unknown; E002 delivers the per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved resources) sourced from notebook-controller activity tracking. In outcome B, BRANCH-B-E005 supplies the readable surface E002 consumes. |\n92\t| HLR-2 | P1 | E003 | Per-project stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from KFP run metadata. |\n93\t| HLR-3 | P2 | E002 (bundled), E003 (bundled) — CSV export is an action on each report's own UI surface over the same report data; it shares the surface and data structures of the P1 report work, so it is not a distinct deferrable feature and a split would touch both report views twice. | Each report epic implements export for its own report. |\n94\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E004 | Documentation of both reports and safe reclamation steps; docs-authoring priority derived from strategy frontmatter `priority: Normal` → P2 (docs-authoring priority exception). |\n95\t\n96\tFull coverage: HLR-1 through HLR-4 all map to at least one epic; no orphaned\n97\trequirements. Out-of-scope items (automated reclamation, cost/chargeback) are\n98\texcluded from all epic scopes.\n99\t\n100\t## Investigation Outcomes and Conditional Branches\n101\t\n102\tE001 has two bounded outcomes:\n103\t\n104\t- **Outcome A — last-activity already readable via the Kubernetes API** (e.g.\n105\t  exposed on the Notebook CR status or an equivalent K8s-readable surface): the\n106\t  main plan proceeds unchanged; E002 reads the existing surface. No branch\n107\t  epics.\n108\t- **Outcome B — not readable today**: BRANCH-B-E005 (Notebooks / Workbenches,\n109\t  P1) exposes per-workbench last-activity on a Kubernetes-readable surface so\n110\t  the console can read it without private component APIs. In this outcome the\n111\t  branch epic completes before E002's data wiring consumes the new surface; its\n112\t  culling behavior must be unchanged. Its `gate_failure_impact` is `remove`: if\n113\t  outcome A holds, the epic does not exist.\n114\t\n115\tE002 carries `gated_by: E001` with `gate_failure_impact.action: rewrite` — if\n116\tthe data is not readable, the report's data-source wiring is rebuilt against\n117\tthe surface exposed by the branch work.\n118\t\n119\t## Health Warnings\n120\t\n121\t- **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n122\t  Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria,\n123\t  and no Non-Functional Requirements; its Affected Components section is a bare\n124\t  list without owner teams or change descriptions. Team assignments in this\n125\t  decomposition are derived from the architecture-context owning teams\n126\t  (dashboard.md, notebooks.md, data-science-pipelines.md).\n127\t- **\"Open Questions: None\" vs. an unresolved data-consumption path**: the\n128\t  strategy asserts the workbench activity data \"exists; it is just not surfaced\n129\t  anywhere\", but dashboard.md states the console's interface is\n130\t  \"Kubernetes API only; no private component APIs\", and notebooks.md describes\n131\t  last activity as \"tracked per kernel through Jupyter server API probes\" by\n132\t  the culler, with no stated CR-status exposure. Whether that tracked value is\n133\t  readable through the Kubernetes API is a genuine unknown that changes which\n134\t  epics exist (it determines whether Notebooks-component work is needed), so it\n135\t  is decomposed as Investigation E001 with a conditional branch rather than\n136\t  taken as resolved.\n137\t- **Documentation team assumption**: HLR-4 is assigned to the RHOAI Dashboard\n138\t  team because the strategy names no documentation owner; reassign if a\n139\t  dedicated docs team owns these topics.\n140\t- **Passive-component validation**: the notebook controller (outcome A) and\n141\t  Kubeflow Pipelines are passive — both are covered by read-only-consumption\n142\t  acceptance criteria on E002/E003 respectively (no behavior changes, culling\n143\t  unaffected), not by separate epics.\n144\t- No priority inversions detected: both P1 HLRs are console reports of\n145\t  comparable complexity; the P2 items (CSV export, docs) are correctly\n146\t  subordinate.\n147\t\n148\t## Tiered Delivery\n149\t\n150\tNot applicable. The strategy has no external dependencies with uncertain\n151\ttiming — all data sources are in-platform components, and no upstream\n152\tcontributions or vendor coordination are required.\n153\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-89bb7d567c197eb1","agent_id":"a1bf09e60a06cbc54","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"578bb4d8-ed17-4944-ac69-084c4d86e0ac","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:29:48.380Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc8402237b7615f7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
