{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be61a855354a5ffa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E003\n3\ttitle: Console stale pipeline-run report with CSV export\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies: null\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Console stale pipeline-run report with CSV export\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the per-project stale pipeline-run report in the RHOAI web\n34\tconsole: an administrator-facing report showing completed pipeline runs older\n35\tthan a configurable age that still retain artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow\n36\tPipelines run metadata (which the platform already retains and already surfaces\n37\tin the console). It also delivers CSV export of the report. Administrators use\n38\tthis report to find old pipeline runs accumulating storage and reclaim capacity\n39\twith confidence; no automated reclamation is performed.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- A new administrator-facing report view in the web console, scoped per\n44\t  project, listing completed pipeline runs older than a configurable age\n45\t  threshold, together with an indication of their retained artifacts.\n46\t- An administrator-configurable age threshold that controls which completed\n47\t  runs count as stale.\n48\t- Data wiring that sources run completion metadata through the console's\n49\t  existing Kubeflow Pipelines integration (KFP v2 run metadata) — read-only\n50\t  consumption, no changes to the Data Science Pipelines component, its\n51\t  operator, or its persistence.\n52\t- A CSV export action on the report that downloads the currently displayed\n53\t  per-project stale-run data.\n54\t- Out of scope: automated reclamation or deletion of runs or artifacts, and\n55\t  cost/chargeback calculations.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a project with completed pipeline runs, the console shows the stale\n60\t  pipeline-run report listing completed runs older than the configured age,\n61\t  with their retained artifacts indicated.\n62\t- The age threshold is configurable, and changing it changes which runs the\n63\t  report lists.\n64\t- The report's data is populated from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata via the\n65\t  console's existing pipelines integration.\n66\t- The Data Science Pipelines component is unchanged by this epic: run\n67\t  execution, metadata retention, and artifact storage behave exactly as before\n68\t  (passive-component validation).\n69\t- Administrators can export the stale pipeline-run report as CSV, and the\n70\t  exported file contains the report's rows and columns.\n71\t- The report is display-only: no reclamation or deletion action is offered.\n72\t\n73\t## HLR Traceability\n74\t\n75\t- **HLR-2 (P1)** — delivers the stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older\n76\t  than a configurable age with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow\n77\t  Pipelines run metadata.\n78\t- **HLR-3 (P2, bundled)** — CSV export of the report is implemented here: the\n79\t  export action lives on this report's own UI surface and shares its data, so\n80\t  it is not separately schedulable from the report itself.\n81\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8a9e06e5ecb2ce0","agent_id":"a0b4c26105ed49c9c","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"8de4abf7-a482-4ae1-8efe-a7a19d77697d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:31:45.360Z","tool_res