{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9138a419d2ba730b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E004\n3\ttitle: Documentation for the idle resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-9016-E002\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9016-E003\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: 1\n19\t  external_dependency: 1\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 6\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# Documentation for the idle resource reports and safe reclamation steps\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers Red Hat documentation explaining the two new console reports\n36\t— the per-project idle-workbench report and the stale pipeline-run report — and\n37\tthe steps administrators can take to safely reclaim the capacity those reports\n38\tsurface. It is authored through the Red Hat docs content process after the\n39\treports are implemented, so the documentation describes what was actually\n40\tbuilt.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- New documentation topics explaining both console reports and safe manual\n45\t  reclamation, covering:\n46\t  - What each report shows (columns: last activity, owner, reserved resources\n47\t    for workbenches; completed-run age and retained artifacts for pipeline\n48\t    runs) and where to find it in the web console.\n49\t  - How to configure the stale pipeline-run age threshold.\n50\t  - How to interpret the reports to identify idle workbenches and stale\n51\t    pipeline runs.\n52\t  - Safe reclamation steps for each resource type, including cautions about\n53\t    data that may be lost and the explicit statement that reclamation is\n54\t    manual (the platform does not automatically reclaim or delete resources).\n55\t  - What is intentionally not covered: automated reclamation and\n56\t    cost/chargeback.\n57\t- Accuracy validation of every documented claim against the shipped reports\n58\t  and against the platform architecture context (console interfaces,\n59\t  notebook-controller activity tracking, Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata).\n60\t- Screenshots and captions that fall out of the documented flows.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- Published documentation explains both reports: what they show, where in the\n65\t  console they appear, and how to read their columns.\n66\t- Published documentation explains how to configure the stale pipeline-run age\n67\t  threshold.\n68\t- Published documentation includes safe reclamation steps for idle workbenches\n69\t  and stale pipeline runs, and clearly states that reclamation is manual.\n70\t- The documentation has been technically reviewed against the implemented\n71\t  reports (reviewed by the implementing engineers) and validated against the\n72\t  platform architecture context before publication.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability\n75\t\n76\t- **HLR-4 (P2)** — delivers documentation explaining the reports and safe\n77\t  reclamation steps.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8a9e06e5ecb2ce0","agent_id":"a0b4c26105ed49c9c","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"60abc511-1798-4b05-87ae-bfc75e633e6c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:31:47.758Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9138a419d2ba730b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
