{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-887febe59084a569","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-BRANCH-B-E005\n3\ttitle: Expose workbench last-activity on a Kubernetes-readable surface\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the investigation finds last-activity is already readable\n16\t    via the Kubernetes API (outcome A), this epic is removed and the console idle-workbench\n17\t    report reads the existing surface directly.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: 0\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Expose workbench last-activity on a Kubernetes-readable surface\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tConditional epic, active only if the workbench-activity data-source\n39\tinvestigation resolves to the outcome where per-workbench last-activity data is\n40\tnot readable through the Kubernetes API today. This epic makes the notebook\n41\tcontroller expose each workbench's last-activity timestamp on a\n42\tKubernetes-readable surface (for example, the Notebook CR status) so the web\n43\tconsole's idle-workbench report can source it through the Kubernetes API\n44\twithout private component APIs. The controller's existing activity tracking and\n45\tidle-culling behavior are preserved unchanged.\n46\t\n47\t## Scope\n48\t\n49\t- Notebook-controller changes that publish the already-tracked per-workbench\n50\t  last-activity value to a Kubernetes-readable surface, following the exposure\n51\t  path recommended by the completed data-source investigation.\n52\t- Population of the exposed value for all workbenches the controller\n53\t  reconciles, kept current as activity probes update it.\n54\t- Preservation of existing culling behavior: the idle culler, its\n55\t  configuration, and its decision logic are unchanged by this work.\n56\t- Out of scope: any console-side reporting work (the console report that\n57\t  consumes this surface is planned in the main plan), and any change to what\n58\t  the controller counts as activity.\n59\t\n60\t## Acceptance Criteria\n61\t\n62\t- Given a running workbench with recorded activity, its last-activity value is\n63\t  readable through the Kubernetes API on the exposed surface, without private\n64\t  component APIs.\n65\t- The exposed value stays current as the workbench is used and goes idle.\n66\t- The idle culler's behavior is unchanged: culling decisions, defaults, and\n67\t  per-workbench overrides behave exactly as before the change (regression\n68\t  check).\n69\t- The console idle-workbench report can populate its last-activity column from\n70\t  the exposed surface.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- **HLR-1 (P1)** — enables: supplies the Kubernetes-readable last-activity data\n75\t  source that the per-project idle-workbench report consumes, in the\n76\t  investigation outcome where no readable surface exists today.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8a9e06e5ecb2ce0","agent_id":"a0b4c26105ed49c9c","session_id":"66891df0-ced6-412e-9fab-8ee1943bcf3f","uuid":"5c158749-1de8-4264-841e-5d83ffe5ed24","timestamp":"2026-10-26T21:31:49.878Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-887febe59084a569","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
